e: Crunchyroll)", "startDate": {"year": 2014, "month": 10}, "endDate": {"year": 2014, "month": 12}, "season": "FALL", "seasonYear": 2014, "episodes": 13, "duration": 24, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": "LIGHT_NOVEL", "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Adventure", "Ecchi", "Fantasy", "Romance"], "tags": [{"name": "Female Harem", "rank": 83, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Magic", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Medieval", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "War", "rank": 78, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "CGI", "rank": 74, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Dragons", "rank": 73, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Archery", "rank": 72, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Male Protagonist", "rank": 70, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Assassins", "rank": 70, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Foreign", "rank": 60, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Heterosexual", "rank": 60, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Swordplay", "rank": 53, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Fugitive", "rank": 40, "isAdult": false}]}, {"id": 20810, "title": {"romaji": "Cardfight!! Vanguard Movie: Neon Messiah", "english": null}, "format": "MOVIE", "description": "After the events of Link Joker-hen, Takuto Tatsunagi announced an invite-only tournament in a dream, and invited both Aichi and Kai to take part in \"Messiah Scramble\". The prize being the card named \"Messiah\", the name of a saviour that was heard in a dream. At the same time, there were many incidents of units disappearing from Vanguard cards throughout the world. Aichi and Kai team up to a confront an enemy that threatens the peace they've just regained.<br>\n<br>\nThe movie is a prequel to Legion, leading up to Aichi's disappearance.", "startDate": {"year": 2014, "month": 9}, "endDate": {"year": 2014, "month": 9}, "season": "SUMMER", "seasonYear": 2014, "episodes": 1, "duration": 72, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": "ORIGINAL", "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Action", "Adventure", "Fantasy"], "tags": [{"name": "Card Battle", "rank": 100, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Male Protagonist", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Idol", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Aliens", "rank": 60, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Demons", "rank": 55, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Alternate Universe", "rank": 20, "isAdult": false}]}, {"id": 20817, "title": {"romaji": "Donten ni Warau", "english": "Laughing Under the Clouds"}, "format": "TV", "description": "When swords were outlawed in the Meiji era, the mighty samurais began to disappear. Those who rejected the ban rebelled, causing unrest throughout the countryside. To combat this criminal activity, an inescapable lake prison was constructed. Three young men, born of the Kumo line, were given the duty of delivering criminals to their place of confinement—but could there be more to their mission? <br><br>\n(Source: Crunchyroll)", "startDate": {"year": 2014, "month": 10}, "endDate": {"year": 2014, "month": 12}, "season": "FALL", "seasonYear": 2014, "episodes": 12, "duration": 24, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": "MANGA", "hashtag": "#donten ", "genres": ["Action"], "tags": [{"name": "Historical", "rank": 90, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Heterosexual", "rank": 80, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Male Protagonist", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Swordplay", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Ninja", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Mythology", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Family Life", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Shoujo", "rank": 76, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Tragedy", "rank": 76, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Military", "rank": 70, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Primarily Male Cast", "rank": 66, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Prison", "rank": 60, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Conspiracy", "rank": 60, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Reincarnation", "rank": 40, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Cute Boys Doing Cute Things", "rank": 20, "isAdult": false}]}, {"id": 20830, "title": {"romaji": "Hi☆sCoool! SeHa Girl", "english": "Hi-sCool! Seha Girls"}, "format": "TV_SHORT", "description": "Three girls meet for the first time at the start of a new semester in a brand new school. But these aren’t just any girls, and this isn’t just any school! Dreamcast, Sega Saturn, and Mega Drive might be the names of SEGA gaming consoles, but at Sehagaga Academy, they’re also three girls destined for greatness! Or at least a nostalgia trip. Wacky hijinks ensue when the girls are tested not on their math and science skills, but on their ability to complete challenges inside (literally!) classic SEGA video games. Can they fight their way through the blocky polygons of Virtua Fighter? Can their dance moves get them high enough ratings in Space Channel 5? And that isn’t all! More challenges await on the road to gaining 100 medals in order to graduate, but the Sega Hard Girls won’t let something like absurdity keep them down!<br><br>\n\n(Source: Discotek)", "startDate": {"year": 2014, "month": 10}, "endDate": {"year": 2014, "month": 12}, "season": "FALL", "seasonYear": 2014, "episodes": 13, "duration": 11, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": "ORIGINAL", "hashtag": "#セハガール", "genres": ["Comedy"], "tags": [{"name": "Video Games", "rank": 100, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Parody", "rank": 88, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "School", "rank": 85, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Full CGI", "rank": 80, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Chibi", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Primarily Female Cast", "rank": 72, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Cute Girls Doing Cute Things", "rank": 70, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Female Protagonist", "rank": 70, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Crossover", "rank": 65, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Henshin", "rank": 60, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Isekai", "rank": 56, "isAdult": false}]}, {"id": 20831, "title": {"romaji": "Cross Road", "english": null}, "format": "SPECIAL", "description": "High school students Miho and Shouta are preparing for college entrance examinations. Miho comes from an island without even one cram school, while Shouta lives in Tokyo and works a part-time job. Both are striving to pass exams so they can enter college. The pair enroll in Z-Kai's correspondence education courses, and their lives cross before they realize it.\n<br><br>\n(Source: Anime News Network)", "startDate": {"year": 2014, "month": 2}, "endDate": {"year": 2014, "month": 2}, "season": "WINTER", "seasonYear": 2014, "episodes": 1, "duration": 2, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": "ORIGINAL", "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Slice of Life"], "tags": [{"name": "School", "rank": 92, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Advertisement", "rank": 87, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Trains", "rank": 68, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Ships", "rank": 60, "isAdult": false}]}, {"id": 20834, "title": {"romaji": "Teekyuu 3 Specials", "english": "Teekyuu 3 Specials"}, "format": "SPECIAL", "description": "Short specials included in the BD release.\n", "startDate": {"year": 2014, "month": 1}, "endDate": {"year": 2014, "month": 1}, "season": "WINTER", "seasonYear": 2014, "episodes": 2, "duration": 2, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": "MANGA", "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Comedy", "Slice of Life", "Sports"], "tags": [{"name": "Aliens", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "School", "rank": 50, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Shounen", "rank": 50, "isAdult": false}]}, {"id": 20835, "title": {"romaji": "ONE PIECE \"3D2Y\": Ace no shi wo Koete! Luffy Nakama to no Chikai", "english": "One Piece 3D2Y: Overcome Ace’s Death! Luffy’s Vow to his Friends"}, "format": "SPECIAL", "description": "This new TV special tells the two years of Luffy's training with Silvers Rayleigh in Rusukaina Island after the Battle of Marineford, which has never been told in the manga or TV anime. It also features a new villain named Burndy World who is known as \"The Destroyer of the World\" and has the power of the MoaMoa Fruit (its ability is still unknown). Luffy has to protect Boa Hancock from the new enemy who escaped from the level 6 of Impel Down. He is newly designed by the original creator of the manga, Eiichiro Oda.<br>\r\n<br>\r\n(Source: Crunchyroll)", "startDate": {"year": 2014, "month": 8}, "endDate": {"year": 2014, "month": 8}, "season": "SUMMER", "seasonYear": 2014, "episodes": 1, "duration": 107, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": "MANGA", "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Action", "Comedy", "Fantasy"], "tags": [{"name": "Pirates", "rank": 100, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Anachronism", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Male Protagonist", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Super Power", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Ships", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Shounen", "rank": 73, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Time Skip", "rank": 20, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Crime", "rank": 20, "isAdult": false}]}, {"id": 20836, "title": {"romaji": "Blade & Soul Specials", "english": null}, "format": "SPECIAL", "description": "Short specials included in the Blade and Soul Blu-rays and DVDs.", "startDate": {"year": 2014, "month": 6}, "endDate": {"year": 2014, "month": 12}, "season": "SUMMER", "seasonYear": 2014, "episodes": 7, "duration": 2, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": "VIDEO_GAME", "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Comedy"], "tags": [{"name": "Female Protagonist", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Chibi", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Primarily Female Cast", "rank": 20, "isAdult": false}]}, {"id": 20837, "title": {"romaji": "Ao Haru Ride: unwritten", "english": null}, "format": "OVA", "description": "Bundled with the 11th volume of the Ao Haru Ride manga. \r\n\r\nEpisode about Futaba and Kou in middle school. Based on the chapter called \"Unwritten.\" also known as chapter 0 or Prologue.", "startDate": {"year": 2014, "month": 8}, "endDate": {"year": 2014, "month": 8}, "season": "SUMMER", "seasonYear": 2014, "episodes": 1, "duration": 22, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": "MANGA", "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Romance", "Slice of Life"], "tags": [{"name": "School", "rank": 79, "is